  "summary": "Required space for placing a boat is too small",
  "environment_raw": "",
  "description": "## The bug\n\nThe required space when placing a boat is too small.\n\nThis allows the collision box of the boat to intersect with blocks.\n\nAt 18w31a will make the boat fall into the void.\n\nVideo:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MlRPQVz-y9Y\n\n## How to reproduce\n\n - Put a boat in your hand\n\n - Place a block on the ground\n\n - Look at the ground right in front of the placed block\n\n - Hold right click while slowly moving the cursor away from the block\n\n## Code analysis\n\nBased on 1.12.2 decompiled using MCP 9.40\n\nThe method net.minecraft.item.ItemBoat.onItemRightClick(World, EntityPlayer, EnumHand) decreases the collision box size when it tests for no collisions:\n\nif (!worldIn.getCollisionBoxes(entityboat, entityboat.getEntityBoundingBox().grow(-0.1D)).isEmpty())\n{\n return new ActionResult<ItemStack>(EnumActionResult.FAIL, itemstack);\n}",
  "Steps to Reproduce": "1. Launch Minecraft 18w31a.\n2. Create a Creative world.\n3. Put a boat in your hand.\n4. Place a block on the ground.\n5. Look at the ground directly in front of the placed block.\n6. Hold the right-click button while slowly moving the cursor away from the block.\n7. Observe that the boat is placed with its collision box intersecting the block, causing the boat to fall into the void.",
  "Environment": "Minecraft Java Edition Versions: 1.9.2, 16w14a, 16w15a, 16w15b, 1.9.3 Pre-Release 1, 1.9.3 Pre-Release 2, 1.9.3 Pre-Release 3, 1.9.3, 1.9.4, 16w20a, 16w21a, 16w21b, 1.10 Pre-Release 1, 1.10 Pre-Release 2, 1.10, 1.10.1, 1.10.2, 16w32a, 16w32b, 16w33a, 16w35a, 16w36a, 16w38a, 16w39a, 16w39b, 16w39c, 16w40a, 16w41a, 16w42a, 16w43a, 16w44a, 1.11 Pre-Release 1, 1.11, 16w50a, 1.11.2, 17w06a, 17w13a, 17w13b, 17w14a, 17w15a, 17w16a, 17w16b, 17w17a, 17w17b, 17w18a, 17w18b, 1.12 Pre-Release 1, 1.12 Pre-Release 2, 1.12 Pre-Release 3, 1.12 Pre-Release 4, 1.12 Pre-Release 5, 1.12 Pre-Release 6, 1.12 Pre-Release 7, 1.12, 1.12.1 Pre-Release 1, 1.12.1, 1.12.2 Pre-Release 1, 1.12.2 Pre-Release 2, 1.12.2, 17w43a, 17w43b, 17w45a, 17w45b, 17w46a, 17w47a, 17w47b, 17w48a, 17w49a, 17w49b, 17w50a, 18w01a, 18w02a, 18w03b, 18w05a, 18w06a, 18w07a, 18w07b, 18w07c, 18w08a, 18w08b, 18w09a, 18w10a, 18w10b, 18w10c, 18w10d, 18w11a, 18w14a, 18w14b, 18w15a, 1.13-pre1, 1.13-pre6, 1.13, 18w31a, 18w32a, 18w33a, 1.13.1-pre1, 1.13.1-pre2, 1.13.1, 1.13.2-pre1, 1.13.2-pre2, 1.13.2, 18w43a, 18w43b, 18w43c, 18w44a, 18w48a, 18w48b, 18w49a, 18w50a, 19w12b, 19w13b, 19w14a, 19w14b, 1.14.3, 1.14.4, 19w34a, 19w39a, 19w42a, 19w45b, 1.15 Pre-release 1, 1.15, 1.15.1, 1.15.2 Pre-release 2, 1.15.2, 20w06a, 20w07a, 20w08a, 20w09a, 20w10a, 20w11a, 20w12a, 20w13b, 20w18a, 1.16 Release Candidate 1, 1.16, 1.16.1, 1.16.2 Pre-release 1, 1.16.2 Release Candidate 1, 1.16.2 Release Candidate 2, 1.16.2, 1.16.3, 1.16.4 Pre-release 1, 1.16.4 Release Candidate 1, 1.16.4, 20w45a, 20w46a, 20w49a, 21w03a, 1.16.5, 21w05a, 21w05b, 21w06a, 21w07a, 21w11a, 21w13a, 21w14a, 21w15a, 21w16a, 1.17 Pre-release 2, 1.17 Pre-release 5, 1.17 Release Candidate 1, 1.17, 1.17.1 Release Candidate 1, 1.17.1, 21w37a, 21w40a, 21w43a (includes snapshots)",
  "Observed Behavior": "## Actual behavior\n\nThe boat can be placed when there is not enough unobstructed space for its full collision box. The placement check uses the boat\u2019s bounding box reduced by `0.1` blocks on each axis:\n\n```java\nentityboat.getEntityBoundingBox().grow(-0.1D)\n```\n\nAs a result, the check may report no collision even though the boat\u2019s actual collision box intersects the block directly in front of the player. The boat is then spawned partially inside the block. In 18w31a, this can cause the boat to fall into the void instead of remaining properly positioned.",
  "Expected Behavior": "When placing a boat near a block, the game should require enough unobstructed space for the boat\u2019s full collision box. If any part of the boat would intersect the nearby block or other solid blocks, placement should fail rather than create the boat in an invalid position. Successfully placed boats should remain properly supported and not fall into the void due to intersecting terrain.",
